# Paint keys on paper, 256x128, fill and stroke forms. Left to right, top to bottom:
# (1) circle with fill:p.red only: red disc, no outline. (2) circle with stroke:p.ink,4 only: a ring of ink 4px thick,
# paper showing through the middle.
# SUSPECT: docs show stroke: alone as a ring (no fill key means no fill) vs the circle renders with a gray
# fill inside the ring (so does stroke:3 in cell 4 and an open path with stroke: only) (3) circle with fill:p.gold and stroke:p.ink,6: gold disc with a thick 6px ink
# outline. (4) circle with stroke:3 alone (width-only): a thin dark ring of 3px, derived from the fill (line(fill)), not
# ink black; same gray inside as cell 2.
# Bottom row: (5) circle with blur:6 filled blue: a soft disc with fuzzy edge, no crisp boundary. (6) the same circle
# with blur:0, crisp edge, for contrast. (7) a green rect 44x44 with name:j1 jitter:1.5,60: the outline is visibly wobbly,
# not a straight-sided square. (8) the same rect with name:j2 jitter:4,30: a stronger, tighter wobble than cell 7.
@target shapes/paint.png 256x128

circle 18 at:32,32 fill:p.red
circle 18 at:96,32 stroke:p.ink,4
circle 18 at:160,32 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,6
circle 18 at:224,32 stroke:3
circle 18 at:32,96 fill:p.blue blur:6
circle 18 at:96,96 fill:p.blue blur:0
rect 40x40 at:160,96 fill:p.green name:j1 jitter:1.5,60
rect 40x40 at:224,96 fill:p.green name:j2 jitter:4,30
